  "term": "modesty",
  "definition": "In historical psychology, modesty is a kind of timidity or shyness that arises from reflective self-consciousness. The term has also been used more loosely for a generally humble or lowly attitude, and it can overlap with feelings such as shame or coyness depending on the situation.",
